WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:07.320
In order to get married in Kenya, the groom's
family has to provide a dowry of at least

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:14.519
10 cows to the bride's family.

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:19.470
Before Beverly Hills was home to the rich
and famous, the area was better known for

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.670
its lima beans.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:28.710
The Vatican City is now home to the Pope and
all his predecessors, but not before the 14th

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.710
century.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.820
Popes used to live in the Lateran Palace in
Rome, and even in France, for a brief period.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:41.090
In the state of Idaho, you are prohibited
by law to go fishing on the back of a camel

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:42.600
or a giraffe.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.760
A building in New York has been built out
of mushrooms.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.370
The mushrooms are grown in a brick mold and
then set in a building.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:58.570
The longest continuous sidewalk in the world
is along Bay Shore Boulevard in Tampa, Florida.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:04.400
In Vermont, billboards are illegal; to ensure
that drivers and passengers can freely admire

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.030
the natural beauty.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:13.100
Andrew Jackson was the only US President to
have the national debt paid in full.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:19.570
The Procrastinators' Club of America newsletter
is called “Last Month's Newsletter.”

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:24.020
Philip Morris once ran an ad acknowledging
“smokers' cough.”

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:29.610
They claimed it was caused by smoking brands
other than Philip Morris.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.650
University of Louisville Police arrested a
man for stealing a book titled "Resolving

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:39.330
Ethical Issues" and trying to sell it to the
bookstore.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:46.850
26 miles of unwrapped steel was used to construct
China's huge “Bird's Nest” stadium—making

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:51.009
it the largest steel structure in the world.

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:56.090
America's first "Air Force" was equipped with
five hot-air balloons and fifty servicemen.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:01.229
New Hampshire is the only U.S. state that
does not lawfully require drivers to wear

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:04.890
safety belts while operating a motor vehicle.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.750
George Washington grew marijuana at his farm.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:14.310
Those doves released at weddings and other
formal ceremonies are actually white homing

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.310
pigeons.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:23.900
True ring-neck doves are bred to be kept as
pets and rarely survive out of captivity.

